  "description": "Version and build ranges as every client and server evaluates them. Versions are SemVer 2.0 with the MAJOR.MINOR and MAJOR shorthands (missing parts 0; prerelease and build only on the full form; build metadata ignored); numbers have no size limit; a version is at most 128 characters after surrounding ASCII spaces and tabs are removed, and contains nothing else outside the grammar. Ranges are comparators (>=, >, <=, <, =) separated by ASCII spaces or tabs, all of which must hold, joined by || alternatives (spaces around || optional; whitespace after an operator optional); a range is at most 1024 characters. Ordering is SemVer precedence (§11) and nothing more, so <2.0.0 admits 2.0.0-beta.1, and a shorthand is an exact version (>1.4 admits 1.4.1, <=1.4 excludes 1.4.5). A version that does not parse matches no range. build_cases use the same comparators over build numbers: 1 to 18 ASCII digits (leading zeros allowed, no sign), so they fit a signed 64-bit integer. invalid_ranges and invalid_build_ranges must be refused. RubyGems requirements are a server-side compatibility form and are not part of this syntax (see legacy_ranges.json).",
